{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JUzcKnRnfugLSfMT4fU97L","type":"tool_result","content":"136:- Components handle all four states: pending / error / empty / success — and every state branch a component owns gets a render test (a state with no test ships broken silently).\n153:- A type or function that gains a second source has every comment on what it holds re-read — a comment written for the one source now states the other's case wrongly, and no check fails when it does.\n157:- **The CSS is the design system** — `src/app.css` (tokens, `panel`/`inset` surfaces) and `src/typography.css` (`tt-*` type scale) are self-documenting and authoritative: tokens only (no color literals), `tt-*` class\n# Plan template\n\nA plan has three parts, and a Research part at its end. The developer reads the Definition\nand the Contract and confirms them before the Build part is written. The executor builds\nfrom all of it.\n\n- The Definition is plain words. A reader who knows the product but not the code can judge\n  it: is this the right thing, and the right approach?\n- The Contract is code and diagrams: what changes for whoever calls it, the models, and how\n  it works. The models are the contract the code is written to.\n- The Research part numbers what the agents were sent to check, E1 and T1, and what came\n  back. A brief is the plan's path and one number, so the plan is written before any agent\n  starts.\n- Each section answers the question in its placeholder, and only that. A task never\n  restates another section. It points at it: a function or a model by name, a requirement\n  by number, a rule or a case by its opening words. A fact written twice gets changed in one\n  place.\n- Fill every section. One with nothing to report says `none`, because \"no migration\" is\n  information. Never leave placeholder text under a heading. The executor will implement\n  it.\n- Write every code block in the codebase's own language. The skeleton shows Python and\n  SQL.\n- The Definition and the Contract name no source file, test, or line of code. The Build and\n  Research parts carry those. A line quoted from the request or a document it links to\n  carries its path:line.\n\n---\n\n````markdown\n# Feature: <feature-name>\n\n# DEFINITION\n\n## Feature Description\n\n<What is it, what is it for, and what is it worth to its users? Two sentences, with no\nfunction or model name.>\n\n## User Story\n\nAs a <type of user>, I want to <action/goal>, so that <benefit/value>.\n\n## Problem Statement\n\n<What is wrong or missing today, for whom, and what shows it?>\n\n## Requirements\n\n<What must the user be able to do, and what must hold, including when its inputs go wrong?\nIn the words a product manager would write: one line each, with no code and no\nGiven/When/Then. Tasks cite them by number (R3), so the numbering is fixed once written.>\n\nR1. <what the user can do, or what must hold>\n\n## Examples\n\n<What will the developer run to judge the build? Two or three real cases, one where\nsomething goes wrong. Tasks cite them by number (Example 2).>\n\n1. <the real case: a record, a day, or a name the developer can look up> → <what the user\nexample.md\nplan-template.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d927ec62-fc1a-4016-9073-c3b01d3098bc","uuid":"5b0e5276-9fdf-421e-9949-8fc0ba4efecb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:58:46.184Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"136:- Components handle all four states: pending / error / empty / success — and every state branch a component owns gets a render test (a state with no test ships broken silently).\n153:- A type or function that gains a second source has every comment on what it holds re-read — a comment written for the one source now states the other's case wrongly, and no check fails when it does.\n157:- **The CSS is the design system** — `src/app.css` (tokens, `panel`/`inset` surfaces) and `src/typography.css` (`tt-*` type scale) are self-documenting and